  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#9285\", \"PowerToys#25062\", \"PowerToys#10337\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before and was closed as by design, not as a regression. When \\\"Hold Shift key to activate zones while dragging\\\" is turned off, FancyZones shows the zones on every drag. The non-primary mouse button option is a toggle, not a hold, so it only switches the zones off or on during a drag. That matches what you see: zones appear by default and the button still toggles them. To get zones only on demand, turn on both \\\"Hold Shift key to activate zones while dragging\\\" and \\\"Use a non-primary mouse button to toggle zone activation\\\" (PowerToys#10337, #9285). With Shift enabled, zones stay hidden until you hold Shift. A setting to start with zones off and only use the mouse button was requested in PowerToys#25062. The archive doesn't show that it was implemented. The tickets don't cover your remark about the start page listing window moving as an activation method, so I can't confirm that part.\"}",
